
Example:
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 300 360 --dec -15 -13 --filter M4376 --non-overlapping --overwrite

Targets must have IN_IBIS=1, IN_HSC!=1, and DONE=0, as well as match the
requested RA, DEC, and filter. HSC targets are excluded before non-overlap trimming.
The input must include IN_HSC so the exclusion can always be applied.
obstatus/cfht-tiles.ecsv is the sole tile catalog; all tile updater scripts
read and write only this ECSV file. Observing plans use FITS and XML.

Target magnitudes use the input tile's EBV_MED:
M4112: MAG_AB = DEFAULT_MAG_AB["M4112"] + 3.774 * EBV_MED
M4376: MAG_AB = DEFAULT_MAG_AB["M4376"] + 3.576 * EBV_MED
Both filter defaults are currently 24.25 in make_cfht_targets.py.
--mag-ab overrides the base magnitude before adding extinction.
This applies to ordinary and nightly plans (FITS/XML and the night schedule).
XML magnitudes are rounded to two decimal places; FITS retains float32 precision.

By default, PROGRAM=LBNL is selected. To select different programs or remove
the restriction (including blank labels), use:
./make_cfht_targets.py --program LBNL
./make_cfht_targets.py --program LBNL NAOC
./make_cfht_targets.py --program ""
./make_cfht_targets.py --all-programs

Program matching ignores case. Future program names are accepted without changing the script;
multiple --program options are combined into one list.

Night planning (requires numpy and astropy; see requirements.txt):
python update_tile_priorities.py
python update_lmst_design.py
python make_cfht_targets.py --night 2026-09-09
python make_cfht_targets.py --night 2026-09-09 --twilight 18 --exptime 150 --overhead 44 --program LBNL

--night is the Hawaii calendar date of the evening. Defaults are 15-degree
twilight, 130-second exposures, and 44-second overheads. Outputs include
evening/morning LMST bounds, FITS/XML queues in time order, and a
targets-YYYY-MM-DD.schedule.ecsv table with every slot and any unfilled slots.
The --lmst-window option sets the allowed LMST_DESIGN mismatch in degrees
(default +/-5 degrees); within that window the highest PRIORITY wins,
with lower declination breaking ties. PRIORITY is assigned from stripe
years (Y1=10.0, Y2=9.0, Y3=8.0, Y4=7.0, Y5=6.0), taking the maximum
where stripes overlap. All IN_IBIS=1 rows are assigned regardless of DONE
or IN_HSC; unassigned stripe locations retain a fallback of 1.0.
See docs/night-planning.md for the design mapping, timing model, and limitations.
Night planning uses local Earth-orientation and leap-second files in data/iers/;
it does not download anything and works with Astropy 4.3.1 or newer.

Repository layout and tests:
The executable scripts and shared night_planning.py module live at the repository
root. Tests live in tests/; documentation, offline reference data, tile catalogs,
and observing plans live in docs/, data/, obstatus/, and plans/, respectively.
Run the full test suite from the repository root (requires requirements.txt):
python -m unittest discover -v
To run a single test module:
python -m unittest -v tests.test_night_planning

Additional targets for NAOC time
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 234 250 --dec 4 10 --filter M4376 --non-overlapping --overwrite --prefix targets-2026-09-08-A --program NAOC
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 307 360 --dec -12 -6 --filter M4376 --non-overlapping --overwrite --prefix targets-2026-09-08-B --program NAOC
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 0 56 --dec -15 -7 --filter M4376 --non-overlapping --overwrite --prefix targets-2026-09-08-C --program NAOC
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 130 225 --dec -7 1 --filter M4376 --non-overlapping --overwrite --prefix targets-2026-09-08-D --program NAOC
./make_cfht_targets.py --ra 307 311 --dec -15 -14 --filter M4112 --non-overlapping --overwrite --prefix targets-2026-09-16 --program NAOC

LBNL scheduled nights
python make_cfht_targets.py --night 2026-09-09 --program LBNL --dec -90 -12 --non-overlapping --overwrite


Uploads to Kealahou:

python upload-plan.py --ot-name OT_M4376_IQ0.6 --run-id NAOC plans/targets-2026-09-08-A.fits
python upload-plan.py --ot-name OT_M4376_IQ0.6 --run-id NAOC plans/targets-2026-09-08-B.fits
python upload-plan.py --ot-name OT_M4376_IQ0.6 --run-id NAOC plans/targets-2026-09-08-C.fits
python upload-plan.py --ot-name OT_M4376_IQ0.6 --run-id NAOC plans/targets-2026-09-08-D.fits
python upload-plan.py --ot-name OT_M4112_IQ0.6 --run-id NAOC plans/targets-2026-09-16.fits
